(THE HUMAN ELEMENT IN STOCK MARKET TRANSACTIONS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The stock market literature of the past thirty years would make a vast) Tj T*
(library in itself--one that would provide reading for a lifetime.) Tj T*
(Perhaps there is no other subject, apart from the eternal topic of) Tj T*
(love, in which more people are vitally concerned, either directly) Tj T*
(or indirectly. Since most of the country?s wealth and commerce is) Tj T*
(controlled by corporations whose securities are listed on the various) Tj T*
(stock exchanges, the price fluctuations, which often reach the daily) Tj T*
(aggregate of hundreds of millions of dollars, either in loss or) Tj T*
(enhancement of value, are necessarily a matter of general concern.) Tj T*
(In 1925 the stock transactions on the New York Stock Exchange alone) Tj T*
(amounted to the stupendous and unprecedented total of well over) Tj T*
(452,000,000 shares, while the sales of listed bonds totaled more than) Tj T*
($3,398,000,000. These figures, of course, do not include the unknown) Tj T*
(billions of dollars worth of securities bought and sold on a dozen or) Tj T*
(more other exchanges and through private channels.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(In addition to the large daily grist of ?Market Opinions,? many books) Tj T*
(and pamphlets are written which purport to be ?Guides to Traders,?) Tj T*
(or up-to-date recipes for ?Beating Wall Street.? They set forth an) Tj T*
(exhaustive array of statistics, instructions and warnings; they) Tj T*
(furnish elaborately charted plans indicating many of the pitfalls of) Tj T*
(speculation; they tell how to avoid these, how to buy, what to buy,) Tj T*
