(the attentive observer; in fact it frequently happens that the) Tj T*
(price fluctuations result from a wave of hysteria among a coterie) Tj T*
(of traders, and bear but little analogy to the true value of the) Tj T*
(stocks. To illustrate this point more explicitly, the stock of almost) Tj T*
(any conservatively capitalized and well managed concern paying six) Tj T*
(dollars annually in dividends has an investment value of from $85 to) Tj T*
($100 a share; but in the ups and downs of the market the stock gets) Tj T*
(buffeted about on the exchange in obedience to the varying sentiments) Tj T*
(of traders, sometimes selling as low as $50, and at other times as) Tj T*
(high as $150, without any change whatever in the company?s earnings,) Tj T*
(its prospects, or its management. \(These matters will be dealt with a) Tj T*
(little farther on, and exemplified by showing their effects upon the) Tj T*
(mentalities of various types of speculators.\) It does not follow that) Tj T*
(one who keeps in touch with the stock market by telephone, or through) Tj T*
(the daily papers, will find his path free from thorns and snares; but) Tj T*
(he will at least have a more open perspective than one who submits to) Tj T*
(the influence of the ticker.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Any intelligent trader may reason out exactly what he ought to do under) Tj T*
(certain specific conditions; but in the quickly shifting and uncertain) Tj T*
(process of determining values he loses his mental poise; and experience) Tj T*
(proves that anyone whose reasoning faculties become confounded is apt) Tj T*
(to be affected by some form of hysteria, and will frequently do the) Tj T*
(opposite of what he would do under normal conditions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The most copious and the most unreliable financial writers are the) Tj T*
(market ?tipsters? who write daily letters of advice to an army of) Tj T*
(subscribers, and claim to have more or less positive knowledge of) Tj T*
(what certain stocks or groups of stocks are going to do marketwise.) Tj T*
(They often profess to have definite ?inside information,? which any) Tj T*
(subscriber may receive at a stated price, ranging anywhere from $10) Tj T*
(a month upward. These false financial prophets, who lead a horde of) Tj T*
(blind followers, should not be confused with reputable bureaus and) Tj T*
(statistical experts who base their opinions and their advice to clients) Tj T*
(upon a logical analysis of general conditions.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
([Illustration]) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Henry Fielding wrote a whole essay to prove that a man can write) Tj T*
(more informingly on topics of which he has some knowledge than on) Tj T*
(matters that he knows nothing about. He believed also that mankind) Tj T*
(is more agreeably entertained by example than by precept; therefore) Tj T*
(it is not the purpose of this discourse to teach anybody anything,) Tj T*
(unless perchance something may be gained by example or suggestion.) Tj T*
(There are four subjects on which advice, however good, is generally) Tj T*
(wasted,--politics, stock speculation, religion, and love; for in these) Tj T*
(matters grown-ups rarely follow the advice of others, and when they do,) Tj T*
(if they profit by it they take all the credit to themselves, whereas if) Tj T*
(they lose they always blame the adviser. Such are the inexorable and) Tj T*
(universal laws of human nature.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
