(their sorrow.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(And still, hundreds of thousands of people continue to play at gambling) Tj T*
(tables, and hundreds of thousands speculate in stocks. There are many) Tj T*
(persons who gamble moderately all their lives, just as some drink) Tj T*
(moderately all their lives, with no resultant harm; while with others) Tj T*
(both of these inhibited practices become fixed and ruinous vices. Since) Tj T*
(trading in stocks has the appearance of being an easy way of making) Tj T*
(money, it is one of the most alluring pursuits of modern times; and) Tj T*
(from this very fact, although legalized for all, it is susceptible) Tj T*
(of becoming one of the most dangerous habits known. It is dangerous) Tj T*
(for the confirmed addict not only because he is apt to lose, but for) Tj T*
(the reason that it distracts his attention from business in daytime) Tj T*
(and frequently destroys his rest at night. But as it would be folly to) Tj T*
(advise people not to embark in commercial pursuits because statistics) Tj T*
(show that upwards of ninety per cent. of business ventures result in) Tj T*
(failure, so it would be useless to caution people not to trade in) Tj T*
(stocks because it is a hazardous undertaking in which a peculiar sort) Tj T*
(of sagacity and self-control are the only safeguards against certain) Tj T*
(disaster.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Most people of sturdy mentality are unwilling to admit that they could) Tj T*
(be made easy subjects of hypnotic influences, and would scout the idea) Tj T*
(that mere business transactions in securities could effect any undue) Tj T*
(subversion of their equipoise. The average human mind is, however,) Tj T*
(incapable of maintaining its equilibrium under the strain of great) Tj T*
(excitement; and no amount of knowledge, either inherent or acquired,) Tj T*
(no amount of experience, however dearly bought, will enable one) Tj T*
(always to think intelligently or act wisely under highly nerve-racking) Tj T*
(conditions. It is said that persons who become disoriented in a forest) Tj T*
(will almost invariably go in the wrong direction \(I have done so myself) Tj T*
(on two different occasions\); and that in an effort to salvage goods) Tj T*
(from a burning house they will throw mirrors and other fragile articles) Tj T*
(out a third-story window and carry pillows downstairs.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(THE DISCONCERTING EFFECT OF SUDDEN LOSSES AND GAINS) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(There are but few things more unbalancing to the mind than the act) Tj T*
(of suddenly winning or losing large sums of money. A few years ago) Tj T*
(at Monte Carlo I was in company with a friend, a well known man of) Tj T*
(affairs who while there played at roulette nearly every day, merely as) Tj T*
(a pastime. He was of mature age, naturally methodical, conservative,) Tj T*
