(temperate and cool-headed. He made it an unalterable rule to limit) Tj T*
(his losses to $200 at any one sitting, and on losing this amount he) Tj T*
(always stopped playing. His bets were usually limited to two dollars) Tj T*
(on the numbers, and never doubled except for one turn of the wheel) Tj T*
(when his number won. He generally played three numbers at a time; never) Tj T*
(more than four. For ten consecutive sittings luck was against him and) Tj T*
(each time he had lost his stake of $200. I saw him get up and leave) Tj T*
(the room, apparently in a state of disgust. An hour or so later I) Tj T*
(discovered him at a roulette table in another room stacking his chips) Tj T*
(in piles on a dozen or more numbers. Now and again when he exceeded the) Tj T*
(limit the watchful croupier reduced his bets and pushed a few disks) Tj T*
(back to him. In addition to betting on the numbers he was staking a) Tj T*
(thousand franc note on one of the three columns, another thousand on) Tj T*
(the colors, and a like amount on the center dozen. In one run he lost) Tj T*
(seventeen consecutive bets on red, of a thousand francs each. His eyes) Tj T*
(were bloodshot, his fingers twitched, and plainly he was under the) Tj T*
(strain of great agitation. He continued to play for three hours or so,) Tj T*
(when all of a sudden he got up, stood for a moment looking dazedly) Tj T*
(about, then left the table. He afterwards told me that he lost twenty) Tj T*
(thousand dollars; and that he hadn?t the slightest recollection of) Tj T*
(anything that happened during the play, nor did he realize the amount) Tj T*
(he was betting. In this connection, it is a fact not generally known,) Tj T*
(that many rich men sign printed cards of instructions to the proprietor) Tj T*
(of a certain well known gambling club in the South, directing him) Tj T*
(to stop their play and refuse them further credit beyond a certain) Tj T*
(specified sum on any one day or evening of play, and refusing to become) Tj T*
(responsible beyond that amount. If men who trade in the stock market) Tj T*
(were to impose like restrictions upon their transactions the losses) Tj T*
(would in many cases be greatly minimized.) Tj T*
