(RETIRED BUSINESS MEN IN THE STOCK MARKET) Tj T*
() Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Retired business men suffering from _ennui_, have often had recourse to) Tj T*
(the stock market as a means of stimulating their emotions and expanding) Tj T*
(their fortunes; with the result, in the first of these purposes they) Tj T*
(have usually succeeded beyond their expectations, while in the second) Tj T*
(they have met with uncharted obstacles. Some years ago when many of) Tj T*
(the great trusts were in process of formation a well known Pittsburgh) Tj T*
(magnate sold out his business to the United States Steel Corporation) Tj T*
(and later bought a home in New York and turned his attention to) Tj T*
(stock speculation. After plunging into a boiling market and buying) Tj T*
(thousands of shares at top prices, the trend eventually changed and he) Tj T*
(found himself on the crest of a tobogganing market with more than a) Tj T*
(hundred thousand shares of speculative stocks. At length when the pace) Tj T*
(threatened both his fortune and his peace of mind, in a fit of disgust) Tj T*
(he dumped his holdings overboard and proceeded to damn the market, the) Tj T*
(broker and everything else, including himself for being such an unlucky) Tj T*
(simpleton.) Tj T*
