(?My dear Mr. Blank,? said his broker, ?you are possibly quite justified) Tj T*
(in all your abuse, except that of yourself, to whom you really should) Tj T*
(apologize, since you do yourself a great injustice. You have had six) Tj T*
(months? experience in this game at an expense of a little less than) Tj T*
(two millions of dollars, whereas at the pace you began you were due to) Tj T*
(lose at least five times that amount but for your rare judgment and) Tj T*
(cool-headedness.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(?But why in hell didn?t you tell me all this before?? inquired) Tj T*
(the irate customer. To which the broker calmly replied, ?It?s my) Tj T*
(business to _take_ orders; not to give directions to a man of your) Tj T*
(understanding.?) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(When the American Hide and Leather Company was formed a number of years) Tj T*
(ago, a prominent Boston leather merchant of my acquaintance, sold) Tj T*
(his business to the new organization for a round million dollars in) Tj T*
(preferred stock and bonds, and in the course of the next few years of) Tj T*
(more or less restless inoccupation he devoted himself to a systematic) Tj T*
(study of investment securities and general stock market conditions. The) Tj T*
(panic of 1907, when values were almost entirely lost sight of in the) Tj T*
(mad scramble to liquidate stocks, afforded a rare opportunity to view) Tj T*
(the follies of reckless speculation, and our astute leather merchant) Tj T*
(was quick to observe the importance of this salutary lesson. The) Tj T*
(recovery that followed was almost magical, and many who bought stocks) Tj T*
(at the low prices doubled their money in a few months. Then following) Tj T*
(this sharp recovery there was the natural setback when speculators) Tj T*
(undertook to convert their new wealth into cash. And this too proved a) Tj T*
(wholesome lesson to our new apprentice in the game of high finance. For) Tj T*
(some years he had held to the conservative practice of investing only) Tj T*
(in non-speculative bonds, but this proved to be a slow and monotonous) Tj T*
(process of enlarging his fortune; furthermore it was devoid of the) Tj T*
(exciting thrills experienced by those who make fortunes overnight. He) Tj T*
(thought the funds of widows and orphans ought properly to be invested) Tj T*
(in gilt edge bonds and mortgages, but for a man of his business) Tj T*
(sagacity, in the prime of life, to content himself with merely cashing) Tj T*
(his coupons every six months was to decline into a state of innocuous) Tj T*
(desuetude--a condition into which he was determined not to retrograde.) Tj T*
(To launch one?s bark into the rapidly shifting currents of fortune in) Tj T*
(the stock market and attempt to steer an even course is one of the) Tj T*
(surest preventives of _ennui_, and after deliberately weighing and) Tj T*
(analysing conditions from every conceivable angle our erstwhile leather) Tj T*
(merchant concluded that cutting a few coupons now and then was too) Tj T*
(tame an occupation for a man of his acumen and ambition. He informed) Tj T*
(his friends that after years of careful study of the ?game,? he was) Tj T*
(convinced that the reason why people lost, was that while in theory) Tj T*
