(It was a wise custom of the ancients to build their pyramids with) Tj T*
(the big end on the ground; but modern builders of pyramids in the) Tj T*
(stock market have reversed this time-honored practice, and most of) Tj T*
(them build their stock pyramids with the heavy end up; therefore they) Tj T*
(invariably topple over after reaching a certain height. For example,) Tj T*
(when a certain stock known as Lake Copper was selling at $5 a share a) Tj T*
