(to sell the whole lot at $15 a share. Before it reached his selling) Tj T*
(price he cancelled the order and raised it to $25; again cancelling) Tj T*
(it and buying another hundred at $25. By this time he was convinced) Tj T*
(that it would go to $50. He bought five hundred more at $40, then the) Tj T*
(stock dropped back, and fearing he might lose all his gains he sold a) Tj T*
(thousand shares at $30. Although he had lost $5000 on the last five) Tj T*
(hundred shares he still had a profit of $4500, less commission, after) Tj T*
(deducting the full cost of the two hundred shares still remaining. The) Tj T*
(stock recovered to $50, and encouraged by the ?street? gossip about) Tj T*
