(way down. The market does not collapse like a ten-story card house;) Tj T*
(it generally goes down gradually for a while, one or two flights at a) Tj T*
(time, and finds steadying props every now and then which sustain it) Tj T*
(for brief periods. For instance, a certain stock paying $5 a share) Tj T*
(annually has been hoisted by degrees from $75 up to $150 a share.) Tj T*
(When it descends to $140 a few wise traders who have been impatiently) Tj T*
