BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738 Td 13 TL
(as it always has periodically in the past---- However, the optimists) Tj T*
(contend that these problems are too far in the future to worry about.) Tj T*
(Furthermore it is not the design of this article to criticise abuses,) Tj T*
(or to prognosticate future difficulties that seem likely to grow out) Tj T*
(of them. It is true that some of the companies, notwithstanding the) Tj T*
(tremendous increase in their capital structures, have not weakened) Tj T*
(their resources by increasing their cash disbursements. In 1921 the) Tj T*
(stock of the Standard Oil Company of New Jersey was paying $5 a year) Tj T*
(in dividends and selling at $124.50 per share. In 1922 it was boosted) Tj T*
(up to $250.50 a share on the report that shareholders were to receive) Tj T*
(four new shares for one. After this split-up was accomplished and the) Tj T*
(authorized common stock increased to 25,000,000 shares,--not dollars,) Tj T*
(but _shares_!--more than 20,000,000 of which have been issued, in) Tj T*
(addition to $200,000,000 of preferred stock, the same conservative) Tj T*
(dividend policy was continued, and the new stock received, and still) Tj T*
(receives, only one dollar a share annually in dividends. The market) Tj T*
(price of the new stock went down to a fraction below $31, whence it) Tj T*
(afterwards recovered to about $46, at which figure it pays a trifle) Tj T*
(over 2%, or about one half the net return on U. S. Government bonds;) Tj T*
(and the only visible change in the stockholder?s position is that if) Tj T*
(he wishes to sell his stock it costs about five times what it did) Tj T*
(before; in other words, to buy and sell the equivalent of one hundred) Tj T*
(shares of the old stock it now costs $154 in commission and tax--more) Tj T*
(than eighteen months? income on a hundred shares of the present stock.) Tj T*
(Possibly there are mathematicians who can figure out some sort of) Tj T*
(compensating advantage to the stockholder, but I never could.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(To sum up the whole situation in a word, those who would make money) Tj T*
(speculating in the stock market should first understand that it) Tj T*
(requires as much caution and business acumen as any other money-making) Tj T*
(enterprise, plus some knowledge of the psychological handicaps; also) Tj T*
(plus the rare faculty of maintaining a complete mastery over one?s) Tj T*
(impulses, emotions and ambitions under the most heroic tests of) Tj T*
(human endurance. All speculations, and even the most conservative) Tj T*
(investments, have some slight element of risk; all lines of business) Tj T*
(are more or less a gamble; marriage is a gamble; political preferment) Tj T*
(is a gamble; in fact nearly everything in life, including our very) Tj T*
(existence, is an uncertainty; yet people are not thereby discouraged) Tj T*
(from entering into any and all of these ventures. Those who look only) Tj T*
(for certainties have far to search and little to find in this world.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(       *       *       *       *       *) Tj T*
() Tj T*
